--- a shared helper's refusal names the export whose call made the copy
--- mistakes: 2
--- `loud` and `quiet` both reach the package's helper `_body_of`, two
--- levels down; the int handed as `quiet`'s `system` makes a copy of the
--- helpers whose `len` meets an int. Every refusal names `say.quiet` at its
--- line: the valid `loud` call, which reaches the helper first, is not
--- blamed (it had been: a copy lowered before its caller's body had no
--- chain on record, and the first export reaching the helper answered).
--- (It had been llm's `chat` and `act`, and before them Magpie's `lookup`
--- and `latest`, until each became a package of its own.)
use say

log[say.loud['be brief']]
log[say.quiet[5]]
